          "comment": "Total overdue actions"
        },
        {
          "name": "avg_days_since_audit",
          "expr": "AVG(last_audit_days_ago)",
          "comment": "Avg days since last audit"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_compliance_score",
          "expr": "MAX(compliance_score)",
          "comment": "Maximum compliance score"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Regulatory Compliance Monitoring for a midstream operator subject to PHMSA pipeline safety regulations (49 CFR 192/195), EPA emissions rules (Subpart W, OOOOb/c), FERC tariff filings, and state-level commission oversight. Stakeholders include the Chief Compliance Officer, VP EH&S, General Counsel (enforcement exposure), and operations leadership (remediation). Industry context: PHMSA NOPV fines average $50K-$250K per violation with maximums above $250K/day; methane rule enforcement is accelerating under EPA's 2024 final rules.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Compliance score = compliance_score on audit_snapshots (0-100; target >90 for low risk)\n- Open findings = open_findings on audit_snapshots; healthy = trending down quarter over quarter\n- Overdue actions = overdue_actions; target = 0 (any overdue triggers escalation)\n- Fines = fine_amount_usd on compliance_events; PHMSA average penalty ~$100K per NOPV\n- Resolution time = resolution_days; PHMSA closure target typically 30-90 days post-finding\n- Violations = violation_count on compliance_kpi_monthly; closure_rate_pct target >95%\n- Training completion = training_completion_pct on compliance_kpi_monthly; OQ rule target 100%\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - compliance_events_metrics (source: compliance_events) — dims: event_date, reg_id, regulatory_body, compliance_area, event_type, severity, status; measures: total_events, total_fines_usd, avg_resolution_days, violation_count, max_fine_amount.\n  - audit_snapshots_metrics (source: audit_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, reg_id, regulatory_body, compliance_area; measures: avg_compliance_score, total_open_findings, total_overdue_actions, avg_days_since_audit, max_compliance_score.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. regulation_name, last_audit_days_ago, closure_rate_pct, training_completion_pct, total_fines_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total fines by regulatory body for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Rank compliance areas by violation count year-to-date.",
    "Which regulations currently have the most overdue actions, and what is the compliance score for each?",
    "How has average resolution days trended month-over-month across PHMSA findings?",
    "Top 10 compliance events by fine amount in the last 6 months.",
    "What is the average compliance score by regulatory body, and which are below 90?",
    "How has closure rate percentage trended monthly across the compliance portfolio?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest fine amount?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(max_fine_amount) AS max_fine_amount",
        "FROM {fqn}.compliance_events_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total fines usd changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(total_fines_usd) AS total_fines_usd",
